Listen to this.

00:04:14.460 --> 00:04:16.380
Я учусь читать по-русски.

00:04:16.820 --> 00:04:19.240
That means I am learning to read in Russian.

00:04:19.600 --> 00:04:22.040
You already know all these school words.

00:04:22.760 --> 00:04:23.120
Amazing.

00:04:23.880 --> 00:04:27.780
Now let's look at a simple grammar idea that ties everything together.

00:04:28.300 --> 00:04:30.720
In Russian, every noun has a gender.

00:04:31.380 --> 00:04:33.540
Think of it like belonging to a team.

00:04:33.540 --> 00:04:37.180
The team changes a little word like my.

00:04:37.980 --> 00:04:41.780
Most nouns ending in a consonant are masculine.

00:04:42.480 --> 00:04:46.980
So we say, Мой учитель, and Мой друг, and Мой урок.

00:04:47.620 --> 00:04:51.520
Most nouns ending in A or Y are feminine.

00:04:52.160 --> 00:04:55.340
So we say, Мойя школа, and Мойя книга.

00:04:55.980 --> 00:04:59.040
In English, we just say the teacher for anyone.

00:04:59.040 --> 00:05:01.660
But Russian picks the right sticker.

00:05:02.100 --> 00:05:04.380
Мой, for masculine nouns.

00:05:05.220 --> 00:05:07.020
Мойя, for feminine nouns.

00:05:07.700 --> 00:05:10.260
Now you can say, Мойя школа, Большая.

00:05:10.720 --> 00:05:15.060
That means my school is big, or Мой друг умный.

00:05:15.600 --> 00:05:17.320
That means my friend is smart.

00:05:18.120 --> 00:05:21.460
You just learned how to much words like a detective.

00:05:22.320 --> 00:05:22.860
Well done.

00:05:23.700 --> 00:05:28.400
In Russia, the first day of school on the 1st of September is a big celebration called

00:05:28.400 --> 00:05:29.560
Дэнснани.

00:05:29.920 --> 00:05:31.780
That means day of knowledge.

00:05:32.200 --> 00:05:36.840
Children bring flowers for their teachers, wear nice clothes, and hear bells ringing at a

00:05:36.840 --> 00:05:37.700
special assembly.

00:05:38.180 --> 00:05:41.460
It shows how much Russian culture respects teachers and learning.

00:05:41.880 --> 00:05:48.220
The teacher is seen as a very important person who helps children grow, just like in all the

00:05:48.220 --> 00:05:49.620
words we learned today.

00:05:50.200 --> 00:05:53.440
Now here is something really cool about one of today's words.

00:05:53.960 --> 00:05:56.140
Want to know a secret about книга?

00:05:57.140 --> 00:06:02.960
Did you know that the Russian word книга and the English word book are actually distant

00:06:02.960 --> 00:06:03.500
cousins?

00:06:04.180 --> 00:06:08.600
They both trace back to ancient words connected to beach trees.

00:06:09.080 --> 00:06:12.800
The very first books were written on thin slices of beach wood.

00:06:13.200 --> 00:06:19.340
The idea started in old languages, traveled through old English as bok meaning beach, while

00:06:19.340 --> 00:06:25.300
a similar word for written record came into Slavic languages as книга around the 10th century

00:06:25.300 --> 00:06:26.820
with early Christian texts.

00:06:27.380 --> 00:06:32.740
But be careful, the Russian word magazine sounds like magazine, but actually means shop.

00:06:33.560 --> 00:06:37.120
That is a fun, false friend that trips up many learners.

00:06:37.780 --> 00:06:42.240
Next time you see the English word book remember it is cousins with книга.

00:06:42.920 --> 00:06:45.500
They both come from the idea of writing on wood.

00:06:46.340 --> 00:06:50.080
That connection is your secret shortcut to remembering it forever.

